// Pre-router "none" cases: messages whose right answer is NO specialist, so the orchestrator keeps the turn.
// SYNTHETIC and hand-labelled; no message comes from a user conversation.
//
// For routing:prerouter only. `"expect": {"admitted": false}` with no agent named is how that bench reads gold none
// (agent/pre-router-bench.ts preRouteGold). routing:eval reads the same field as "the embedding admits nothing", a
// different question: a multi-step chain may well admit the specialists of its parts. Do not add this file to a
// routing:eval run.
//
// Three kinds, tagged:
//   direct-answer    small talk, the assistant itself, a concept, a calculation on given numbers, a short rewrite or
//                    translation: the orchestrator answers in its own reply, no tool, no lookup.
//   clarify          the goal or the input is missing and nothing in the message supplies it: only the orchestrator
//                    can ask back; any specialist would guess.
//   multi-step-chain two short steps for two different specialists, the second depending on the first: a
//                    single dispatch does half the job. These are short chains the orchestrator plans itself, not
//                    the decompose-and-merge missions the catalog's coordinators exist for (those name a coordinator
//                    in live-cases.jsonl).
//
// Run: pnpm --filter @starlingai/core routing:prerouter -- --backend readout --cases eval/routing/live-cases.jsonl --cases eval/routing/none-cases.example.jsonl
